# Draft a one-page spending decision brief — learner brief

Fictional Northstar Services training material.

## Approved fictional facts
F1 September budget USD 200,000.
F2 actual USD 218,000; supplied variance USD 18,000 / 9%.
F3 approved explanation USD 12,000 contractor extension and USD 6,000 travel.
F4 forecast revision proposed, unapproved.
F5 operations lead must confirm remaining contractor end date by September 25.
## Supplied options
D1 maintain support one month, estimated incremental USD 8,000.
D2 reduce support, estimated two-week delay.
D3 controller recommends D1; CFO decision requested September 26. Neither option approved.
D4 revenue effect unknown. Estimates are fictional writing inputs.


## Task

Northstar's controller has already evaluated two responses to a contractor extension. Prepare a brief for the CFO.

## Actions


1. Identify the approved observations and separately list estimates and unknowns.
2. Ask AI to propose an outline before drafting.
3. Draft a brief up to 350 words using only the supplied options and recommendation.
4. Check that the unknown revenue effect remains explicit and estimates stay labeled.
5. Prepare a three-sentence oral summary containing the same decision request.


## Output
Headline; facts; supplied options table; recommendation attributed to controller; unknowns; CFO decision request.
